<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 57,040 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 57,040 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 57,040 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Saturday compared to 81,459 tonnes in the same period on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Saturday    May 23</p>
<p>    Export cargo		30,008	13,251</p>
<p>    Import cargo		27,032	68,208</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and one berthed. In the next 24 hours, four are expected to sail and 13 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		60,000	 CSP - 10		  24/5</p>
<p>Vegoil		 18,000	 Ariston		   Due</p>
<p>Crude oil	    50,795	 Johar		     25/5</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     50,000	 Al - Marwah	     26/5</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     30,000	 Ying Song Hu	    30/5</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
